body: "## What happens\n\nWhen a tracker item exists under the ID the importer reserves for an issue (`<prefix>-github-<hash>-<N>`) but was not created by the importer, the gated import refuses to run for the whole repository:\n\n> GitHub import target pm-vcs-github-c1741e698b48-228 is reserved for unbraind/pm-vcs#228, but its current owner is curated/unowned for content mirroring; importer creation provenance missing. Restore the intended GitHub provenance only if this item belongs to that issue; otherwise use a different configured ID prefix or tracker. …\n\nThis happened in three repositories on 2026-11-26 (pm-vcs issue 228, pm-rl issue 202, pm-ado issue 137): while the sync was down, agents that fixed those issues created the tracker item by hand under the reserved ID and tagged it `gh:owner/repo#N`.\n\n## What works (verified)\n\nSetting the declared field on the item links it explicitly, and the import then matches it by provenance:\n\n```\npm update <item> --field github_url=https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/issues/<N>\npm github import <owner>/<repo> --state all --atomic --gate --dry-run   # plan verified, 1 matched by provenance\n```\n\n`--adopt-cited` alone does not help, and `pm github identity --identity … --owner …` needs a `--detach`, which does not fit a single item.\n\n## Expected\n\n1. The refusal names the repair: \"set `github_url` on this item to link it, or …\".\n2. The documentation for people and agents who start work on an issue says how to get its item: `pm github import <owner>/<repo> --issue <N>` (creates it with provenance), never a hand-created item under the reserved ID form.\n3. Optional: `pm create` refuses or warns when the requested ID matches the importer's reserved form and no `github_url` is set.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- The refusal text contains the repair command for the named item.\n- Tests: a hand-created item under the reserved ID with `github_url` set is matched; without it the refusal names the repair."
